## Widget Architecture

- Prefer composition over inheritance
- Keep widgets immutable
- Use `StatelessWidget` when possible
- Create small reusable widgets
- Avoid deep widget nesting
- Extract widgets to private classes
- Never return widgets from methods
- Follow @lib/features/shared/widgets/ patterns

## Constructor Patterns

- Always use `super.key` constructors
- Use `const` constructors everywhere
- Pass keys through widget tree
- Initialize final fields in constructor
- Use named parameters for clarity
- Apply factory constructors when needed
- Keep constructors simple and focused

## Build Method Practices

- Keep `build()` methods small
- Avoid expensive operations in `build()`
- No network calls in `build()`
- Extract complex UI to widgets
- Use `const` constructors everywhere
- Cache expensive computations
- Minimize widget rebuilds

## Color and Opacity Patterns

- Use `withValues()` instead of deprecated APIs
- Apply `Color.withValues(alpha: 0.5)` for transparency
- Extract colors to theme constants
- Use `Theme.of(context).colorScheme` for colors
- Define semantic color meanings
- Test colors in light/dark modes
- Maintain accessibility contrast ratios

## Performance Optimization

- Use `const` for static widgets
- Apply `ListView.builder` for long lists
- Implement `SliverList` for custom scrolling
- Use `RepaintBoundary` for expensive widgets
- Apply `AutomaticKeepAliveClientMixin` carefully
- Run expensive ops with `compute()`
- Profile with Flutter DevTools

## Widget Organization

- One widget per file
- Group widgets by feature
- Create widget libraries
- Use barrel exports
- Keep widgets focused
- Separate logic from UI
- Follow @lib/features/shared/widgets/ structure

## Widget Composition

```dart
// Monica app widget pattern with super.key
class AppLoadingWidget extends StatelessWidget {
  const AppLoadingWidget({this.message, this.size = 32, super.key});

  final String? message;
  final double size;

  @override
  Widget build(BuildContext context) {
    final ThemeData theme = Theme.of(context);

    return Center(
      child: Column(
        mainAxisSize: MainAxisSize.min,
        children: <Widget>[
          SizedBox(
            width: size,
            height: size,
            child: CircularProgressIndicator(
              strokeWidth: 3,
              color: theme.colorScheme.primary,
            ),
          ),
          if (message != null) ...<Widget>[
            const SizedBox(height: 16),
            Text(
              message!,
              style: theme.textTheme.bodyMedium,
              textAlign: TextAlign.center,
            ),
          ],
        ],
      ),
    );
  }
}
```

## Modern Flutter Patterns

- Use spread operators `...` for conditional widgets
- Apply `if` statements inside widget lists
- Use `Theme.of(context)` for theming
- Extract theme data to variables
- Use `ColorScheme.fromSeed()` for Material 3
- Apply proper Material 3 elevation
- Follow Monica brand color patterns

## Common Widget Patterns

- Use `Builder` for context access
- Apply `LayoutBuilder` for responsive UI
- Use `FutureBuilder` for async data
- Apply `StreamBuilder` for streams
- Use `ValueListenableBuilder` for simple state
- Implement error boundaries
- Add loading states @lib/features/shared/widgets/loading_widget.dart
- Handle empty states @lib/features/shared/widgets/empty_state_widget.dart